"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever","html_url":"https://github.com/Arbee4ever","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arbee4ever/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T08:04:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T08:04:57Z","body":"So, after looking at the code and finding out that the call to `protocol.start(port, IPAddress(host))` returned the error 22 (ERR_ALREADY_IN_USE), I found out, that there was an instance of godot still running in the background, without me being able to see it. I only found it using `lsof -i :6005 -S` in the Terminal. After killing that instance using the System Monitor, it works again. This should probably be improved be either logging errors for the `protocol.start` method or automatically trying other ports when this error is detected (naturally also logging these attempts). I'll see if I can make a PR in the coming days to implement something like this","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3833578772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3834374687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115722#issuecomment-3834374687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115722","id":3834374687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ki-of","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T10:49:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T10:49:05Z","body":"> This should probably be improved be either logging errors for the `protocol.start` method or automatically trying other ports when this error is detected\n\nDoing proper logging about it seems alright. But I see no benefit in trying other ports, because the external editor won't be aware of those.\n\nLoosely related: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95125","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3834374687/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]